WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.317
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid.

2
00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:07.785
Every case is a brand new story, and you are
the detective.

3
00:00:08.835 --> 00:00:12.163
Each puzzle is a logic grid wrapped in a
story.

4
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:16.182
The story sets up a mystery, the clues give
you the facts,

5
00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:19.277
and the grid is where you work out the answer.

6
00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:24.402
Every story is written fresh for you and never
repeated.

7
00:00:24.752 --> 00:00:29.574
And every puzzle has exactly one answer you
can reach without guessing.

8
00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:35.297
New to logic puzzles? Press How to play, at
the top of every page.

9
00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:39.765
It teaches you to solve them step by step, on
real grids.

10
00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:47.066
Five short lessons take you from your very
first mark to solving a whole puzzle on your
own.

11
00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:49.288
They cover every kind of clue,

12
00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:53.241
carrying facts across the grid, what-if
thinking, and hints.

13
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:58.707
Each step explains one idea, then you make the
marks yourself.

14
00:00:59.057 --> 00:01:01.602
The game tells you when a mark does not fit,

15
00:01:01.622 --> 00:01:04.861
and Show me makes the marks for you if you are
stuck.

16
00:01:05.911 --> 00:01:10.370
Tips and tricks puts the moves that solve most
puzzles on one page.

17
00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:16.343
In a hurry? Play a quick puzzle starts a small
Easy case straight away,

18
00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:18.183
with no choices to make.

19
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:24.205
Every day there is also a new Daily puzzle,
the same one for everyone.

20
00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:27.009
Solve it each day to build a streak.

21
00:01:28.059 --> 00:01:32.219
With a free sign-in, you can get each day's
puzzle by email.

22
00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:38.243
Anyone can get the puzzle of the week and
special edition puzzles by email,

23
00:01:38.263 --> 00:01:39.478
with no account.

24
00:01:39.828 --> 00:01:43.275
Choose Puzzle emails in the Menu, type your
address,

25
00:01:43.295 --> 00:01:46.378
then press Confirm in the email we send you.

26
00:01:47.428 --> 00:01:49.071
Here's how to play.

27
00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:53.663
Start on the New puzzle screen and pick a
difficulty.

28
00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.129
Basic and Easy are perfect for beginners.

29
00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:00.551
Quantum Physicist is for true masterminds.

30
00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:04.699
And Theoretical Physicist is for the best of
the best.

31
00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:08.506
Next, choose a theme. Themes are grouped,

32
00:02:08.526 --> 00:02:12.875
like Mystery and Action, Imagination, or
Science and Learning.

33
00:02:13.225 --> 00:02:15.039
Or pick Surprise me.

34
00:02:16.089 --> 00:02:20.071
Most themes also open a list of topics right
under them,

35
00:02:20.091 --> 00:02:23.386
like which holiday or which kind of mystery.

36
00:02:23.736 --> 00:02:25.785
Pick one, or leave it on Any.

37
00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:28.414
Then pick a size.

38
00:02:28.764 --> 00:02:32.882
More categories and more items make a bigger,
harder grid.

39
00:02:33.932 --> 00:02:38.925
Under More options, Full experience adds
scenes, characters and sound.

40
00:02:39.275 --> 00:02:44.310
Silent mode keeps only the story, the grid,
the clues and the answer key.

41
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.435
Press Generate puzzle, and your story is
written in a moment.

42
00:02:50.485 --> 00:02:53.899
Here's our case: The Campfire Golden Paddle.

43
00:02:54.249 --> 00:02:57.365
The buttons along the top help you as you
play.

44
00:02:58.415 --> 00:03:00.165
Read the story first.

45
00:03:00.515 --> 00:03:05.763
It tells you who is involved, and it ends with
the question you need to answer.

46
00:03:06.113 --> 00:03:09.101
Here, it's: Who woke up at 6:30 AM?

47
00:03:09.451 --> 00:03:12.865
You can also press Read the story aloud to
hear it.

48
00:03:13.915 --> 00:03:19.654
Every character has a personality, shown under
their name, and a voice of their own.

49
00:03:20.004 --> 00:03:25.231
Select a character's portrait to hear the
clues they remember, in their own words.

50
00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:28.227
Every clue is also in the clue list.

51
00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:33.246
To hear every clue in order, press Read the
clues aloud.

52
00:03:33.596 --> 00:03:38.311
Each character tells their own clue, and the
clue being read lights up.

53
00:03:39.361 --> 00:03:44.034
While a voice reads, the character who is
speaking appears in the corner.

54
00:03:44.384 --> 00:03:50.507
When AI pictures are on, they get a lifelike
face, and their lips move with their words.

55
00:03:50.857 --> 00:03:54.097
They act the part too: a nervous witness
fidgets,

56
00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:58.325
a cheerful one smiles, and a caught culprit
hangs their head.

57
00:03:58.675 --> 00:04:01.619
You can turn Talking faces off in Settings.

58
00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:08.601
On your first Easy puzzle, coach tips appear
above the grid to guide your first moves.

59
00:04:09.651 --> 00:04:11.017
Now the grid.

60
00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:16.167
Each square is where two things meet, like a
camper and a wake-up time.

61
00:04:16.517 --> 00:04:19.910
Your job is to decide whether they go
together.

62
00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.905
Click or tap a square once to mark an X.

63
00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:27.818
X means ruled out: these two don't go
together.

64
00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:33.221
Tap again for an O. O means confirmed: these
two are a match.

65
00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:36.046
Tap a third time to clear the square.

66
00:04:37.096 --> 00:04:40.958
Let's solve it together, starting with the
simplest clues.

67
00:04:41.308 --> 00:04:45.213
Clue 1 says Wren did not wake up at 6:50 AM.

68
00:04:45.563 --> 00:04:47.185
Mark an X there.

69
00:04:48.235 --> 00:04:52.161
Clue 2 says Juniper woke up at 6:40 AM.

70
00:04:52.511 --> 00:04:54.047
Mark an O there.

71
00:04:55.097 --> 00:04:58.533
Clues 3 and 4 each rule out pairs directly.

72
00:04:58.883 --> 00:05:00.846
Mark an X for each one.

73
00:05:01.896 --> 00:05:05.502
Clue 5 says Arlo sleeps in Firefly Cabin.

74
00:05:05.852 --> 00:05:07.389
Mark an O there.

75
00:05:08.439 --> 00:05:14.124
Clue 6 says the camper who sleeps in Owl Cabin
did not wake up at 7:00 AM,

76
00:05:14.144 --> 00:05:19.383
and the camper who sleeps in Owl Cabin did not
wake up at 6:50 AM.

77
00:05:19.733 --> 00:05:21.355
Mark an X there.

78
00:05:22.405 --> 00:05:27.814
Arlo sleeps in Firefly Cabin, so Arlo cannot
go with any other cabin,

79
00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:31.131
and no other camper can go with Firefly.

80
00:05:31.481 --> 00:05:35.775
Each row and each column in a section has
exactly one match,

81
00:05:35.795 --> 00:05:38.821
so everything else in that line is an X.

82
00:05:39.871 --> 00:05:45.280
Arlo sleeps in Firefly Cabin, so Arlo cannot
go with any other cabin,

83
00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.597
and no other camper can go with Firefly.

84
00:05:49.647 --> 00:05:55.743
Juniper woke up at 6:40 AM, so Juniper cannot
go with any other wake-up,

85
00:05:55.763 --> 00:05:59.311
and no other camper can go with 6:40 AM.

86
00:06:00.361 --> 00:06:04.501
6:30 AM is the only wake-up left for Arlo.

87
00:06:04.851 --> 00:06:06.387
Mark an O there.

88
00:06:06.737 --> 00:06:11.837
When only one square is left in a row or
column, it must be the answer.

89
00:06:12.887 --> 00:06:18.199
In the full experience, each finished section
also reveals more of the scene.

90
00:06:19.249 --> 00:06:20.807
Stuck? Press Hint.

91
00:06:21.157 --> 00:06:26.107
The first hint shows you which clue to use,
and names the trick that cracks it.

92
00:06:27.157 --> 00:06:32.427
Press Which cell? for the exact square, then
Explain why for the full reasoning.

93
00:06:32.777 --> 00:06:36.233
It ends with a short lesson on how that trick
works,

94
00:06:36.253 --> 00:06:38.943
so you can spot it yourself next time.

95
00:06:39.293 --> 00:06:42.238
You can even let it mark the square for you.

96
00:06:43.288 --> 00:06:47.470
Press Check at any time to see whether any of
your marks are wrong.

97
00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:54.025
Made a mistake? Undo and Redo take back any
move, as many times as you like.

98
00:06:55.075 --> 00:06:58.041
Want a fresh start? Press Start over.

99
00:06:58.391 --> 00:07:02.359
It clears your marks and resets the timer,
hints and checks.

100
00:07:02.709 --> 00:07:08.278
Your notes stay unless you choose to clear
them, and Undo can bring everything back.

101
00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:14.257
Prefer words to grids? List view lets you
choose each match from a menu.

102
00:07:14.607 --> 00:07:18.639
The game also works fully by keyboard and with
a screen reader.

103
00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:24.789
When you think you know, answer the questions
under the clues, and press Check answers.

104
00:07:25.839 --> 00:07:29.530
Want to jot something down? Press My notes and
type.

105
00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.742
Press Save to keep them, or Close to get back
to the puzzle.

106
00:07:34.092 --> 00:07:37.229
Only you can see your notes, even in a race.

107
00:07:38.279 --> 00:07:43.101
Keep going the same way, clue by clue, until
the whole grid is filled in.

108
00:07:44.151 --> 00:07:45.474
Case closed!

109
00:07:45.824 --> 00:07:52.886
Arlo woke up at 6:30 AM, and Arlo only hid the
golden paddle as part of a prank war.

110
00:07:53.236 --> 00:07:57.397
You also see your time and a suggestion for
your next puzzle.

111
00:07:58.447 --> 00:08:02.157
Every solve ends with a celebration, like
confetti,

112
00:08:02.177 --> 00:08:05.765
fireworks, ribbons, balloons or shooting
stars.

113
00:08:06.115 --> 00:08:10.745
Silent mode and your device's reduce motion
setting turn it off.

114
00:08:11.795 --> 00:08:15.593
Solving puzzles earns badges, like First case
closed.

115
00:08:15.943 --> 00:08:19.860
Press Share my result to send friends a
picture of your win.

116
00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.130
It never gives the answers away.

117
00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:28.109
Challenge a friend makes a link to this very
puzzle, with your time to beat.

118
00:08:28.459 --> 00:08:32.491
Your friend needs no account, and you both see
who was quicker.

119
00:08:33.541 --> 00:08:38.673
If you like, rate the puzzle from 1 to 5
stars, where 5 is excellent,

120
00:08:38.693 --> 00:08:43.099
and say whether it felt too easy, just right
or too hard.

121
00:08:43.449 --> 00:08:44.418
It is optional.

122
00:08:44.438 --> 00:08:49.402
The game learns from your answers and tunes
your next puzzle to suit you.

123
00:08:50.452 --> 00:08:56.469
You can print any puzzle, blank or with your
marks, with the answer key on its own page.

124
00:08:57.519 --> 00:09:00.015
Your progress saves automatically.

125
00:09:00.365 --> 00:09:05.102
Come back any time and pick up where you left
off, from Saved puzzles.

126
00:09:06.152 --> 00:09:10.661
My stats and badges, in the Menu, shows your
totals, best times,

127
00:09:10.681 --> 00:09:15.006
favorite themes, your daily streak and every
badge to earn.

128
00:09:16.056 --> 00:09:18.894
Press Help to see every keyboard shortcut.

129
00:09:19.944 --> 00:09:24.702
And Introduction, at the top of every page,
plays this video again.

130
00:09:25.752 --> 00:09:27.929
Play in light or dark colors,

131
00:09:28.979 --> 00:09:30.857
or in high contrast.

132
00:09:31.907 --> 00:09:36.195
And Silent mode is always there when you just
want the puzzle.

133
00:09:37.245 --> 00:09:42.473
Prefer a simpler screen? Use the Basic and
Interactive switch at the top.

134
00:09:42.823 --> 00:09:47.602
The game opens on Interactive, the full look
you have seen so far.

135
00:09:48.652 --> 00:09:52.946
Basic is the game's first, classic look: flat
white panels,

136
00:09:52.966 --> 00:09:58.381
a blue accent and a plain, easy-to-read font,
with no screen animations.

137
00:09:58.731 --> 00:10:03.798
You play exactly the same way, and every clue
is open from the start,

138
00:10:03.818 --> 00:10:06.475
with no picture puzzles to unlock.

139
00:10:07.525 --> 00:10:13.078
Everything else is here too: every theme and
topic, drawn pictures, voices,

140
00:10:13.098 --> 00:10:18.449
races and the scoreboard, stats and badges,
hints, saves and printing.

141
00:10:18.799 --> 00:10:22.042
Only the talking faces stay in Interactive.

142
00:10:22.392 --> 00:10:27.726
The game remembers your choice, and
Interactive switches you back at any time.

143
00:10:28.776 --> 00:10:33.662
To play without opening a browser, choose
Install the app from the Menu.

144
00:10:34.012 --> 00:10:38.514
Download the Windows desktop app, which keeps
itself up to date.

145
00:10:38.864 --> 00:10:42.617
Or add the game's icon to your phone's home
screen.

146
00:10:42.637 --> 00:10:45.969
On your phone, the same menu shows you how.

147
00:10:46.319 --> 00:10:52.485
On a phone, pull down from the top of the page
to refresh. Your progress is saved first.

148
00:10:53.535 --> 00:10:56.202
You can also play with other detectives.

149
00:10:57.252 --> 00:10:59.685
You never need an account to play.

150
00:11:00.035 --> 00:11:02.559
But a free account keeps your puzzles,

151
00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:07.886
progress and settings in step on the website,
the desktop app and your phone.

152
00:11:08.936 --> 00:11:11.966
The name at the top shows who you are playing
as.

153
00:11:12.316 --> 00:11:15.005
Until you sign in, you play as Guest.

154
00:11:16.055 --> 00:11:18.807
Create one with your email and a password.

155
00:11:19.157 --> 00:11:23.855
Keep me signed in is ticked, so you stay
signed in on this device.

156
00:11:23.875 --> 00:11:26.241
Untick it on a shared computer.

157
00:11:26.591 --> 00:11:31.797
If you ever forget your password, Forgot
password sends you a reset link.

158
00:11:32.847 --> 00:11:36.559
Once you are signed in, your puzzles sync on
their own.

159
00:11:36.909 --> 00:11:40.643
Sign in on another device and they are waiting
for you.

160
00:11:41.693 --> 00:11:47.301
Signed in, Printable puzzle pack in the Menu
prints a few brand-new puzzles at once,

161
00:11:47.321 --> 00:11:49.011
with their answer keys.

162
00:11:49.361 --> 00:11:52.429
Pick how many, the difficulty and the theme.

163
00:11:52.449 --> 00:11:55.826
Each player gets a set number of packs a week.

164
00:11:56.876 --> 00:12:00.077
Once you are signed in, you pick a screen
name.

165
00:12:00.427 --> 00:12:05.163
Type your own, or press Suggest a name and the
game makes one up for you.

166
00:12:05.513 --> 00:12:10.357
It is the only thing other players see, and
rude names are turned away.

167
00:12:10.707 --> 00:12:14.462
Don't want one? Sign out instead, and you play
as Guest.

168
00:12:15.512 --> 00:12:18.179
Your screen name now shows at the top.

169
00:12:18.529 --> 00:12:23.497
Play against others lets you race other
players on the very same puzzle,

170
00:12:23.517 --> 00:12:25.399
and climb the scoreboard.

171
00:12:26.449 --> 00:12:28.562
To race, press Start a race.

172
00:12:28.912 --> 00:12:34.310
It uses the difficulty, theme and size you
picked on the New puzzle screen.

173
00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.198
Share the race code or link with a friend.

174
00:12:38.548 --> 00:12:42.453
Or anyone can press Find a race to join an
open race.

175
00:12:43.503 --> 00:12:46.042
Everyone gets the very same puzzle.

176
00:12:46.392 --> 00:12:51.171
The race bar shows the code, and Standings
shows who is still solving.

177
00:12:52.221 --> 00:12:54.590
When you finish, you see your place.

178
00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:58.546
Fastest solve wins, and each hint adds time.

179
00:12:59.596 --> 00:13:03.202
The scoreboard ranks players this week and of
all time.

180
00:13:03.552 --> 00:13:07.521
Every solve earns points, even when you play
on your own.

181
00:13:07.871 --> 00:13:12.437
Press Scoring and race rules to see exactly
how points are awarded.

182
00:13:13.487 --> 00:13:17.583
This week's leaders are always in view at the
top of the page.

183
00:13:17.933 --> 00:13:20.622
Select Scoreboard there to see the full board.

184
00:13:21.672 --> 00:13:27.177
To race one particular player, press Challenge
a player and type their screen name.

185
00:13:28.227 --> 00:13:33.603
They see your challenge under Play against
others, the next time they open the game.

186
00:13:33.953 --> 00:13:39.138
Accept starts the race on the very same
puzzle. No thanks turns it down.

187
00:13:40.188 --> 00:13:42.322
Finally, make the game your own.

188
00:13:43.372 --> 00:13:49.303
In Settings, sound effects and theme music
start on, and you can turn either one off.

189
00:13:49.653 --> 00:13:53.387
Learn from how I play tunes your next puzzles
to suit you.

190
00:13:54.437 --> 00:13:56.465
And play in your own language.

191
00:13:56.815 --> 00:14:03.429
US English is the default, and you can choose
any of 100 languages under Language.

192
00:14:03.779 --> 00:14:06.375
The game translates itself as you play,

193
00:14:06.395 --> 00:14:10.905
and the English button at the top shows the
original at any time.

194
00:14:11.955 --> 00:14:15.326
Have an idea for a story, or found a problem?

195
00:14:15.676 --> 00:14:19.831
Ideas and problems, in the menu, has a
separate box for each,

196
00:14:19.851 --> 00:14:22.738
and they go straight to the game's team.

197
00:14:23.088 --> 00:14:27.398
For a storyline idea, pick which theme it is
for from the list.

198
00:14:27.748 --> 00:14:32.414
Signed in with a confirmed email? Leave Email
me an update ticked.

199
00:14:32.434 --> 00:14:37.413
The game emails you a thank-you, and again
when the team acts on it.

200
00:14:37.763 --> 00:14:41.347
Want an answer? Tick Let the team reply to me.

201
00:14:42.397 --> 00:14:47.433
When the team writes to you, or posts news,
the Menu button shows a number.

202
00:14:48.483 --> 00:14:53.155
Messages, in the menu, has news from the
game's team for everyone.

203
00:14:53.505 --> 00:14:57.240
Signed in, you can write to the team with a
question,

204
00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:01.378
an idea or a problem, and read their replies
right here.

205
00:15:01.728 --> 00:15:06.059
Tick Email me, and you get a short email when
the team writes back.

206
00:15:07.109 --> 00:15:11.825
Dream up a character of your own with Suggest
a character, in the menu.

207
00:15:12.175 --> 00:15:17.210
Answer a few questions about their name, look,
personality and voice.

208
00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:22.851
The game's team reviews every suggestion, and
you might meet yours in a puzzle.

209
00:15:23.901 --> 00:15:29.662
That's all you need: read the story, follow
the clues, and mark your X's and O's.

210
00:15:30.012 --> 00:15:34.151
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid. Happy
sleuthing!

